## Phase 1 — One truth: “printed” vs “not done” ✅

### Shipped
| Piece | Behaviour |
|--|--|
| `PrintJobLifecycle` | Shared states: **queued → sending → printed / failed / needs_attention** |
| Queue DB | `pending` / `printing` / `completed` / `failed` / **`needs_attention`** (retries exhausted) |
| Enqueue | = **queued** only — not physical printed |
| Physical printed | Queue `completed` after `SendToPrinter` OK (+ online ACK waits for that) |
| Kitchen revision / send tracking | Enqueue success → **`queued`**, not `printed`; next Send only retries **failed / needs_attention** lines |
| Receipt reprint | Returns true only when job id queued |
| Visibility | `GetNotPrintedVisibleJobsAsync` / `CountNeedsAttentionAsync` + queue snapshot includes Needs attention; Retry Failed resets needs_attention too |

**Done when:** failed/unclear stays not printed and is visible in print queue (Needs attention) ✅

## Phase 2 — Queue + auto-retry when printer ready ✅

### Shipped
| Piece | Behaviour |
|--|--|
| `FlushWaitingJobsForPrinterAsync` | On ready: clear backoff; re-queue **pending + failed + needs_attention** for **that printer only**; kick queue process |
| `PrintReliabilityCoordinator` | Subscribes `PrinterStatusChanged` (offline→online); starts 30s health probe |
| Kitchen lifecycle | `JobCompleted` → promote revision/send **queued/needs_attention → printed** when no other kitchen jobs waiting for that order |
| Needs attention | Max retries / permanent fail → queue `needs_attention` + kitchen lines marked; ready-flush resets attempts |
| Coverage | Kitchen/bar/kitchen_takeaway routes, online tickets (existing queue + ACK), customer receipts — same durable queue |
| Status column | Migrate to `VARCHAR(32)` so `needs_attention` is accepted |

**Done when:** load new paper → last failed kitchen/receipt/online ticket reprints without staff hunting the order (in normal cases) ✅

## Phase 3 — Staff UI (Mother) ✅

### Shipped
| Piece | Behaviour |
|--|--|
| **Print problems** dialog | Printer Setup → Manage Queue — Failed / Needs attention list |
| Row fields | Order # · type (Kitchen / Receipt / Online) · printer · time · status |
| **Retry** | Same job back to pending (no second copy) |
| **Reprint** | Confirm “may duplicate” → new queue job + dismiss original |
| **Dismiss** | Reason required → cancelled with audit |
| Bulk | Retry all failed · Cancel previous days · Cancel all waiting |
| Ready toast | `Printer ready — retrying N failed ticket(s)…` (~4.5s) |

**Done when:** Manager can fix a miss in one place without opening every order ✅

## Phase 4 — Client + online edges ✅

### Shipped
| Piece | Behaviour |
|--|--|
| Client print | Still via Mother only; Mother down → clear refuse (“tap Send/Print again when Mother is back”) |
| Client reconnect | **No** pending-flush queue (Phase 0) — staff Send/Print again |
| Online/web | Same durable queue + ready-retry; **CAS** printed ACK so both tickets completing never double-ACK |
| Advance kitchen | `advance_kitchen_queued_at` on enqueue; **once-stamp + popup only after JobCompleted** |
| Advance miss→paper | Queued jobs wait for Phase 2 ready-flush; stale queued cleared if jobs gone |

**Done when:** Client and web behave like Mother for “miss then paper change” ✅

## Phase 5 — Safer status (where printer allows) ✅

### Shipped
| Piece | Behaviour |
|--|--|
| ESC/POS DLE EOT | Probe paper / cover / error before send when the printer replies |
| Paper out / cover / error | Do **not** mark printed — retry (then Needs attention); health treats as not-ready so paper load → ready-flush |
| No status reply | Honest target: TCP send still allowed; rare duplicate/miss accepted |
| Labels | Skip DLE (no false paper blocks) |
| Support log | AppData `print-reliability.log` — job id, printer, attempts, outcome, last error, status detail |

**Done when:** better printers get fewer false “printed”; weak printers still auto-retry on ready ✅

## Phase 6 — QA (real till + real paper) ← you

Code paths ready (Phases 0–5). **Manual till + real paper still required** — code alone cannot ✅.

| # | Check | Expect | Code path |
|--|--|--|--|
| 1 | Pull paper mid-kitchen print | Job not left as silent success; ends failed / needs attention or retries | DLE probe → retry; no `completed` on paper-out |
| 2 | Load new paper | Last failed kitchen ticket auto-prints | Health not-ready→ready → `FlushWaitingJobsForPrinterAsync` |
| 3 | Same for receipt | Last failed receipt auto-prints | Same queue + flush for that printer |
| 4 | Online order + paper out | Auto-retry when ready; not lost for the day | Queue hold + ready-flush; ACK only after both jobs complete |
| 5 | Printer offline then back | Queue flushes failed for **that printer only** | `PrinterStatusChanged` offline→online |
| 6 | Client Mother down | Clear fail; reconnect = staff Send/Print again (Phase 0 — no Client pending-flush) | `ClientOfflinePolicy` Print / Advance refuse |
| 7 | Manual reprint | One ticket; warn possible duplicate | Print problems → Reprint confirm |
| 8 | Never | Auto-reprint all open tables / whole day | Flush scoped to `printer_id` only |
| 9 | Max retries | Visible Needs attention — not invisible lose | Queue + Print problems list |
| 10 | Duplicate case | At most same ticket twice, not a flood | Ready-flush same jobs; reprint is explicit |

### How to run (ops)
1. Restart Mother after build (coordinator + health probe running).
2. Use a real kitchen + receipt printer (and online path if testing #4).
3. Optional: watch AppData `print-reliability.log` for job id / attempts / paper status.
4. Client (#6): turn Mother off → Send/Print refuse → bring Mother back → staff Send/Print again.

**Done when:** checklist passed on real Mother + printers (+ Client if used). Not ✅ until you run it.

